    <area>gateway.reports</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>7</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Rewards</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The last ten dives in the Archive; "◄ Gateway" brings you back here.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_terminal_back</defName>
    <label>Back</label>
    <area>terminal.back</area>
    <screen>Any</screen>
    <order>0</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Start_Terminal</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Back to the Core (or to the Gateway when you came from there). Esc closes the terminal.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_retreat</defName>
    <label>Retreat</label>
    <area>dive.retreat</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>7</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Dive</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Leave the dive early. From the lobby it is free; deeper you lose part of the haul.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_tiles</defName>
    <label>Menu tiles</label>
    <area>menu.tiles</area>
    <screen>Menu</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Settings</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Continue goes back where you were. Settings: events and interface. Cyberpedia: how it all works (NEW counts unread articles). Achievements, difficulty and the terminal's look.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_status</defName>
    <label>Net status</label>
    <area>menu.status</area>
    <screen>Menu</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Heat and its level, awake AIs, runners in the net and the cyberdata in storage, at a glance.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_footer</defName>
    <label>Version and reports</label>
    <area>menu.footer</area>
    <screen>Menu</screen>
    <order>3</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Settings</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The mod's version. «Copy diagnostics» puts versions, mods and the state of the game into the clipboard for a bug report. Esc closes the menu.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_settings</defName>
    <label>Settings</label>
    <area>menu.settings</area>
    <screen>MenuSettings</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Settings</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>How often events come, how many AIs turn up, the map size, newcomer protection, the dive summary and the pause on opening. The look and the sound are in Customization.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_achhead</defName>
    <label>Progress</label>
    <area>menu.achhead</area>
    <screen>MenuAchievements</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Settings</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>How many goals are done and the points they gave. With Vanilla Achievements Expanded they also show in its Netrun tab.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_achgrid</defName>
    <label>Achievements</label>
    <area>menu.achgrid</area>
    <screen>MenuAchievements</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Settings</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Each card shows the goal and the progress. Secret ones show themselves when done. A lock marks a reward: a frame theme for the terminal.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_difficulty</defName>
    <label>Difficulty</label>
    <area>menu.difficulty</area>
    <screen>MenuDifficulty</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Pick a preset: Newcomer, Normal, Hard or Cyberpunk. Every slider can be moved on its own: trace growth, cooling, ICE and patrols, AI hunger, scrub price, loss on retreat. Any change makes it «Custom».</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_customtabs</defName>
    <label>Customization tabs</label>
    <area>menu.customtabs</area>
    <screen>MenuCustomization</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Settings</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Frame: the casing's theme and parts. Sound: the sound pack and volumes. Graphics: colours, animations, glitches, CRT lines, text and icon size.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_menu_custompage</defName>
    <label>The page</label>
    <area>menu.custompage</area>
    <screen>MenuCustomization</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Settings</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Changes apply at once and are saved when the terminal closes. Frame themes open with achievements; the rest is free.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_defense</defName>
    <label>Colony defense</label>
    <area>gateway.defense</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>7</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Picking Home shows the colony's defense: the total and its parts, the ICE tier and its upkeep, the firewalls and the honeypot, isolation and intrusions on the way. Everything about the defense is set here.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_panel</defName>
    <label>Side panel</label>
    <area>gateway.panel</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Runners and pods ready to connect, the watchlist, the next three days, then the picked hub: its nodes, the route and the dive. Home shows the colony defense.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_searchbox</defName>
    <label>Search</label>
    <area>gateway.searchbox</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>10</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Type a hub, node or corporation (F). Enter jumps to the first hit. Keys: H home, R or Tab the next runner, 0 the whole map.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_lenses</defName>
    <label>Lenses</label>
    <area>gateway.lenses</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>11</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Keys 1-6 recolour the map: everything, loot, danger, corporations, jobs, travel time from the selected runner. The scale shows in the lower left.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_minimap</defName>
    <label>Minimap</label>
    <area>gateway.minimap</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>12</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The whole net; the frame is your view. Click or drag to jump.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_watchlist</defName>
    <label>Watchlist</label>
    <area>gateway.watchlist</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>13</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Hubs you watch (right click on a hub) and contract targets. «Show» centres the map on one.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_timeline</defName>
    <label>Next 3 days</label>
    <area>gateway.timeline</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>14</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>What ends or starts soon: transit windows, patrols, storms, the corporate core, intrusions. A row centres its hub.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_studio_main</defName>
    <label>The Studio</label>
    <area>studio.main</area>
    <screen>Studio</screen>
    <order>0</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Braindance</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Raw recordings from your colonists turn into braindance chips here: edit them, mix moods, sell or play them.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_board_list</defName>
    <label>The Board</label>
    <area>board.list</area>
    <screen>Board</screen>
    <order>0</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Fixers_Contracts</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Offers from your fixers and the contracts you run: their goal, time, reward and what failing costs. A contract with a target on the map has «Show».</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

</Defs>
